  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466448",
      "title": "Adding an Auth Guard",
      "lectureOrder": 631,
      "videoOrder": 582,
      "sourceHash": "c94bfa722966d561d651d90c00a4aef1a409aa2687c4ac14aa12338ea54bb266",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 4.29,
          "en": "Instructor: So how can we prevent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.29,
          "end": 7.53,
          "en": "that users can visit slash recipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.53,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "if they are not authenticated?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 12.69,
          "en": "Do you remember the routing section?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 14.49,
          "en": "There we had a look at route guards,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.49,
          "end": 16.44,
          "en": "and that is exactly what we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 19.53,
          "en": "A route guard allows us to run logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.53,
          "end": 21.84,
          "en": "right before a route is loaded,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.84,
          "end": 25.23,
          "en": "and we can deny access if a certain condition is not met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.23,
          "end": 27.84,
          "en": "And this is exactly what we need here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.84,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "For that, in the auth folder, let's create a new file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 34.62,
          "en": "and I'll name it auth.guard.ts and that will be my,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.62,
          "end": 38.493,
          "en": "well as the name suggests, authentication guard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 42.177,
          "en": "And in there, let's export a class AuthGuard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.68,
          "end": 48.68,
          "en": "which should implement the canActivate interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 51.03,
          "en": "Now this is imported, not from this path,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.03,
          "end": 55.05,
          "en": "but from @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.05,
          "end": 57.21,
          "en": "And since this technically is a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.21,
          "end": 58.29,
          "en": "and of course you could name it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.29,
          "end": 61.29,
          "en": "export class AuthGuard service therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.29,
          "end": 64.35,
          "en": "Since this is a service, we need @Injectable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.35,
          "end": 66.93,
          "en": "whoops, injectable, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.93,
          "end": 69.27,
          "en": "which is imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.27,
          "end": 72.39,
          "en": "And here you can use providedIn root",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.39,
          "end": 74.82,
          "en": "to provide this application wide if you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.82,
          "end": 78.81,
          "en": "Again, you could also add it to providers in the app module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.81,
          "end": 80.73,
          "en": "So that is the authGuard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 83.73,
          "en": "Since we add the canActivate interface here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 86.55,
          "en": "we now have to add the canActivate method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "The canActivate method has to be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 92.31,
          "en": "implemented in a certain way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.31,
          "end": 94.25999999999999,
          "en": "It receives the currently active route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 96.723,
          "en": "which is of type ActivatedRouteSnapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.83,
          "end": 98.94,
          "en": "And you can, by the way, see this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.94,
          "end": 102.53999999999999,
          "en": "if you press command or control and click on the interface.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.53999999999999,
          "end": 104.49000000000001,
          "en": "Then you can see the definition here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.49000000000001,
          "end": 105.75,
          "en": "So we get two arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 105.75,
          "end": 110.34,
          "en": "the ActivatedRouteSnapshot, and the RouterStateSnapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.34,
          "end": 111.59899999999999,
          "en": "So that's the second thing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 111.59899999999999,
          "end": 116.59899999999999,
          "en": "RouterStateSnapshot, both imported from @angular/router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.52000000000001,
          "end": 124.52,
          "en": "And canActivate then has to return either a Boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 129,
          "en": "or a promise that eventually yields a Boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129,
          "end": 132.84,
          "en": "expressed here by using this generic promise notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 137.64,
          "en": "or an observable which eventually will yield a Boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.64,
          "end": 141.753,
          "en": "And for that you also need to import Observable from RXJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.13,
          "end": 145.5,
          "en": "This is how canActivate should look like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.5,
          "end": 148.71,
          "en": "and right now we're getting an error because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.71,
          "end": 151.29,
          "en": "we are not returning anything when we are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.29,
          "end": 155.52,
          "en": "expected to return a Boolean, a promise, or an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.52,
          "end": 157.62,
          "en": "Now what can we return here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.62,
          "end": 160.86,
          "en": "We wanna return the status as we can derive it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.86,
          "end": 165.03,
          "en": "from our auth service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.03,
          "end": 170.03,
          "en": "So here let's inject the authService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.31,
          "end": 172.29,
          "en": "which is of type authService in which you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.29,
          "end": 175.23,
          "en": "need to import from the authService file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.23,
          "end": 178.5,
          "en": "And then in there we can find out whether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 180.51,
          "en": "the user is authenticated or not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.51,
          "end": 184.08,
          "en": "by looking at that user behavior subject.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.08,
          "end": 188.52,
          "en": "So here we can access this authService user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 188.52,
          "end": 191.52,
          "en": "and now don't subscribe here, but return it instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.52,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "because this already is an observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 194.28,
          "end": 197.01,
          "en": "It's a subject and therefore also an observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 199.65,
          "en": "however not an observable that returns a Boolean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.65,
          "end": 201.03,
          "en": "Instead it is an observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.03,
          "end": 203.4,
          "en": "that in the end returns a user object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.4,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "but this can be fixed easily.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 209.73,
          "en": "We just add pipe and use the map operator, which is imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.73,
          "end": 214.71,
          "en": "from RXJS operators, to transform the observable value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.71,
          "end": 218.16,
          "en": "So we get our user, and we wanna return true or false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 218.16,
          "end": 219.27,
          "en": "so we can simply return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 219.27,
          "end": 221.64,
          "en": "exclamation mark exclamation mark user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.64,
          "end": 223.41,
          "en": "which is that trick which converts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 223.41,
          "end": 226.56,
          "en": "a true-ish value like a, object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.56,
          "end": 228.66,
          "en": "so anything that is not null or undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.66,
          "end": 231.12,
          "en": "to true, so to a real Boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 231.12,
          "end": 233.76,
          "en": "or that converts a false-ish value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.76,
          "end": 236.76,
          "en": "like null or undefined to a true Boolean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 236.76,
          "end": 238.68,
          "en": "so to false in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 238.68,
          "end": 241.44,
          "en": "So now we have an observable that really will return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 241.44,
          "end": 243.87,
          "en": "true or false, and that should allow us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.87,
          "end": 245.64,
          "en": "to use that activate guard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 245.64,
          "end": 248.493,
          "en": "in front of the routes that we wanna protect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.63,
          "end": 252.243,
          "en": "So now with canActivate added here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 253.08,
          "end": 255.66,
          "en": "let's go to the app routing module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 255.66,
          "end": 258.9,
          "en": "And here of course it's this path here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 258.9,
          "end": 261.78,
          "en": "the recipes path, which I wanna protect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.78,
          "end": 264.99,
          "en": "So in there we can add the canActivate key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 264.99,
          "end": 267.69,
          "en": "which is an array of all the can activate guards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 267.69,
          "end": 269.43,
          "en": "you wanna register for this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 272.22,
          "en": "and here it's only one route, it's the auth,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 272.22,
          "end": 274.23,
          "en": "only one guard it's the authGuard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 276.28,
          "en": "which you also need to import, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 278.1,
          "end": 281.1,
          "en": "With that change, let's save that and let's see if it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 282.3,
          "end": 283.53,
          "en": "That doesn't look too bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 283.53,
          "end": 285.36,
          "en": "We are kind of stranded here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 285.36,
          "end": 287.07,
          "en": "and we should take care about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.07,
          "end": 290.31,
          "en": "but at least we can't access slash recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 290.31,
          "end": 293.1,
          "en": "Though, is this really the right behavior?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 293.1,
          "end": 295.29,
          "en": "Let's have a look at application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 295.29,
          "end": 300.12,
          "en": "This is empty, so let's try logging in now like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 300.12,
          "end": 301.59,
          "en": "And we can visit recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 301.59,
          "end": 304.53,
          "en": "So here we are granted access, this looking good,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 304.53,
          "end": 308.67,
          "en": "and now let's reload the recipes page, and this also works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 308.67,
          "end": 311.64,
          "en": "So indeed this works and it gives us the right data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 311.64,
          "end": 314.04,
          "en": "The guard works correctly here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.04,
          "end": 316.92,
          "en": "What we should make sure though, is that when we log out,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 316.92,
          "end": 319.86,
          "en": "and we manually try to go to slash recipes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 319.86,
          "end": 322.62,
          "en": "that we actually redirect the user to a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 322.62,
          "end": 325.59,
          "en": "where he can do something like the authenticate page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 325.59,
          "end": 328.86,
          "en": "And to do that we can go back to the guard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 328.86,
          "end": 333.57,
          "en": "In there we are returning true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 333.57,
          "end": 335.31,
          "en": "But now if we have a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 335.31,
          "end": 336.69,
          "en": "at the canActivate interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 336.69,
          "end": 339.18,
          "en": "by command or control clicking on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 339.18,
          "end": 340.486,
          "en": "we see we can actually return more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 340.486,
          "end": 343.95,
          "en": "than just observables or promises or Booleans.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 343.95,
          "end": 347.15999999999997,
          "en": "We can although return a URL tree,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 347.15999999999997,
          "end": 351.06,
          "en": "or a promise, or an observable that yields a URL tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 351.06,
          "end": 353.94,
          "en": "This is a relatively new feature and it was added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 353.94,
          "end": 357.27,
          "en": "basically for this exact use case, for authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 357.27,
          "end": 360.42,
          "en": "It was added so that you can redirect users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 360.42,
          "end": 363.81,
          "en": "when the URL they're trying to visit is blocked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 363.81,
          "end": 365.73,
          "en": "So for canActivate for this guard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 365.73,
          "end": 370.47,
          "en": "which you often use in connection with authentication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 370.47,
          "end": 373.77,
          "en": "you have now a more convenient way of redirecting users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 373.77,
          "end": 376.95,
          "en": "In the past, with older angular versions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 376.95,
          "end": 378.84,
          "en": "you had to manually redirect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 378.84,
          "end": 381.36,
          "en": "So for example, here you would've added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 381.36,
          "end": 386.283,
          "en": "a tap RSJX operator, which you need to import by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 387.51,
          "end": 390.36,
          "en": "And there you would get that is of information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 390.36,
          "end": 392.79,
          "en": "because map gives us true or false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 392.79,
          "end": 394.65,
          "en": "is the user authenticated or not?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 394.65,
          "end": 395.94,
          "en": "And then here you could check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
